From 56890ecab6d20e4d50fa9928fb30a6bff8a92c51 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pascal Garber <pascal@artandcode.studio>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 14:48:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] libcamera: software_isp: Correct static phase detection
 pixels

The Sony IMX376 delivers its phase-detection pixels uncorrected. In
every 16x16 tile eight blue sites, (1,1) (9,1) (5,5) (13,5) (5,9)
(13,9) (1,13) (9,13), read 1.4-1.8x their same-colour neighbours; all
other sites are within 0.2%. The sensor cannot be told to correct them.

SwStatsCpu samples one 2x2 block out of every four columns, so half of
its blue samples are such pixels. AWB then computes a blue gain of ~1.3
instead of ~1.9 and the image turns yellow-green. The debayered image
also shows a faint grid of blue dots.

Describe the pixels in CameraSensorProperties, valid only for the
output size they were measured on, and add PdafPixelCorrector, which
replaces each site by the rounded mean of its in-frame same-colour
neighbours at +-2. It supports 10-bit CSI-2 packed, 8-bit and 16-bit
container raw, and is precomputed at configure time.

The correction runs in Debayer::process() on the ISP worker thread, on
the input mapped read/write and DMA-synced ReadWrite, before the
statistics and debayering, for both the CPU and EGL back ends. For EGL
the sync ends right after the correction, flushing the CPU writes
before the dmabuf is imported by the GPU.

Assisted-by: AI coding agent
